# Python CI lint gate

CI jobs `python-lint` and `python-typecheck` run exactly:

```bash
ruff check .
ty check --error-on-warning
```

Path-filtered ruff or ty is not a valid CI substitute.

Before every Python commit or push, run `bash scripts/check-python-ci-lint.sh` against the whole repo. That script runs the CI ruff/ty pair **and** `pytest tests/test_hardcoded_ids.py` (shrink-only guard against new `User(id=<int>)` / `user_id=<int>` test literals and new `user_id=1` in `app/`). Re-run after every later Python edit. A green run from before the last edit does not count. Do not use `--no-verify`.

Never add bare integer primary-key Call keywords in tests (`user_id=1`, `User(id=1)`). Use fixture-owned IDs. See `.cursor/rules/hardcoded-ids.mdc` and `AGENTS.md` (“Test identity validation”).

Before the first Python commit of a session, run `bash scripts/install-git-hooks.sh` so Cursor's remapped `core.hooksPath` can still chain to `.git/hooks/pre-commit`.
